---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Copyright And Intellectual Property"
  description="Ownership, permitted use, attribution, and rights information for Leverage AI website content."
  canonicalPath="/intellectual-property"
>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="shell surface stack prose legal-page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Last updated June 30, 2026</p>
      <h1>Copyright and intellectual property</h1>
      <p>
        Unless otherwise identified, the original writing, page design, graphics, code, reports,
        and other creative material published on leverageai.network are owned by Leverage AI LLC or
        used with permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Case-study and client materials</h2>
      <p>
        Client and project names, trademarks, product names, screenshots, photographs, and other
        materials remain the property of their respective owners. Their appearance in a case study
        documents work performed or provides commentary; it does not transfer ownership to
        Leverage AI.
      </p>

      <h2>Permitted use</h2>
      <p>
        You may link to public pages and quote brief excerpts for commentary, education, or
        discussion when you identify Leverage AI as the source and link to the original page.
        Broader reproduction, republication, resale, model training, or creation of substantially
        similar commercial materials requires prior written permission unless the use is otherwise
        allowed by law.
      </p>

      <h2>No ownership of facts or ideas</h2>
      <p>
        Copyright protects original expression, not facts, ideas, systems, methods, or general
        business concepts. References to public research or industry methods do not claim ownership
        over the underlying facts or ideas.
      </p>

      <h2>Permission and concerns</h2>
      <p>
        To request permission, report a possible rights issue, or ask for attribution details,
        email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Include the page URL and enough
        information to identify the material.
      </p>

      <h2>Official resource</h2>
      <p>
        Learn more from the <a href="https://www.copyright.gov/help/faq/faq-protect.html">United States Copyright Office</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
